# Local build knobs for the native wrapper. Copy to `native/.env` (gitignored,
# and kept out of the EAS upload by .easignore) and fill in what you need.
# Nothing here is required for a normal build.

# The EAS project this app builds under. `eas init` prints the id but cannot
# write it into a dynamic config (app.config.js), so it is passed in instead.
# CI reads it from the EAS_PROJECT_ID repository secret.
# WHERE: https://expo.dev -> the project -> its overview page, or `eas init`.
# SHAPE: a lowercase UUID, 8-4-4-4-12.
# EAS_PROJECT_ID=

# An Expo access token, for driving EAS with no interactive login. A laptop
# uses `eas login` instead; CI reads it from the EXPO_TOKEN repository secret.
# WHERE: https://expo.dev/settings/access-tokens (personal), or
# https://expo.dev/accounts/<account>/settings/access-tokens (robot — the right
# kind for CI, since it cannot sign in to the dashboard and owns no projects).
# Treat it as a password.
# EXPO_TOKEN=

# Points the WebView at a deployed slot instead of the copy of the app bundled
# inside it. DEBUGGING ONLY — a store build that streams the website is the
# exact shape App Store guideline 4.2 rejects.
# VALUE: any URL the device can reach — a deploy slot on the live origin, or a
# dev server on the LAN (http://<your-lan-ip>:5173/, not localhost, which on a
# phone means the phone).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_PAINT_URL=https://paint.niclaslindstedt.se/preview/
